{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicitySelfDualToSymplectic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicitySelfDualToSymplectic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.Classical","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.SymplecticGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_embedding_of_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_embedding_of_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicitySelfDualToSymplectic.lean#L108-L130","doc":"**CONDITIONAL downstream — `𝔰𝔩₂` embedding from self-duality.**\n\nGiven the (open) Tannakian premise `SelfDualToSymplectic (Fin 1) R g` and the\nproved coincidence `sp_fin_one_eq_sl`, the automorphism Lie algebra `g` lands\ninside `𝔰𝔩(Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 1) R`. Feeding that into the landed rank bound\n`QOU.Atomicity.sl2_subalgebra_rank_le_one` (PR #4285) — threaded here as the\nexplicit hypothesis `sl2_rank_le_one`, so this file stays decoupled from that\nunmerged branch — yields the downstream conclusion `P`.\n\nThe only unproved input is the class instance itself; everything else is fully\nverified by Lean. This is the §3b-cond conditional-on-class pattern: the class\ncarries a genuine hypothesis (`g ≤ 𝔰𝔭`) and the theorem *derives* its conclusion\nrather than assuming it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.SelfDualToSymplectic.embeds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.SelfDualToSymplectic.embeds","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicitySelfDualToSymplectic.lean#L106-L106","doc":"The automorphism Lie algebra `g` of the self-dual fundamental object is a\nLie subalgebra of the symplectic Lie algebra of its duality pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.SelfDualToSymplectic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.SelfDualToSymplectic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicitySelfDualToSymplectic.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.SelfDualToSymplectic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.SelfDualToSymplectic","kind":"class","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicitySelfDualToSymplectic.lean#L85-L106","doc":"**OPEN (Tannakian premise) — self-duality forces a symplectic structure.**\n\n`SelfDualToSymplectic l R g` axiomatises the categorical input that the\nautomorphism Lie algebra `g` of a *self-dual* fundamental object embeds into the\nsymplectic Lie algebra `Symplectic.sp l R` of its nondegenerate antisymmetric\nduality pairing. The single field `embeds` is the *real* mathematical statement\n(`g ≤ 𝔰𝔭`), not `True`.\n\nThis is genuinely open in the corpus: it is a Tannaka-duality claim about the\nfibre functor on a rigid symmetric monoidal category with a symmetric duality,\nnot a theorem proved in this file. Per AGENTS.md §\"Axiomatization is NOT a Proof\"\nand §3b, the open state is represented by the **absence of an instance** — the\nclass is uninhabited. No `sorry` and no fabricated instance appear: providing an\ninstance would *be* the proof, which is not available.\n\nRef (manuscript, not yet formalised): `def:tannaka-dual`,\n`def:fundamental-object`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sp_fin_one_eq_sl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sp_fin_one_eq_sl","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicitySelfDualToSymplectic.lean#L40-L83","doc":"**Low-rank coincidence `𝔰𝔭(2) = 𝔰𝔩(2)` (`C₁ = A₁`).**\n\nThe symplectic Lie subalgebra of `Matrix (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 1) (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 1) R`,\ndefined as the skew-adjoint matrices for the rank-one symplectic form\n`J = fromBlocks 0 (-1) 1 0`, coincides *exactly* with the special-linear Lie\nsubalgebra of trace-zero matrices.\n\nProof: membership in `Symplectic.sp (Fin 1) R` unfolds (via\n`mem_skewAdjointMatricesLieSubalgebra` and `mem_skewAdjointMatricesSubmodule`)\nto `J.IsSkewAdjoint A`, i.e. `Aᵀ * J = J * (-A)`; membership in\n`SpecialLinear.sl (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 1) R` is definitionally `trace A = 0`. Reducing\nthe matrix equation entrywise over `Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 1` shows both are equivalent to\n`A (inl 0) (inl 0) + A (inr 0) (inr 0) = 0`, the trace-zero condition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}